    "name": "Sedum Rupestre \"Blue Spruce\"",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The Sedum Blue Spruce is a succulent ground cover with small, fleshy blue leaves reminiscent of the needles of a blue spruce conifer. In summer, deep mauve-pink stems topped with brilliant yellow flowers rise to about 25 cm. Planted into a plastic baggie in a berry pint. You can remove the plastic bag and plant the berry pint into the dirt as it will break down.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Contains 5 starter stalks.</span></p>",
